    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052857_312768_101018" xmi:uuid="c81212b5-4208-4804-8314-86cef22d3fce" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1608111407753_790148_95075" xmi:uuid="d164fa06-e383-4686-903a-356b49801f3f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052857_312768_101018"/>
        <body>A TotalRunoutTolerance is a type of GeometricTolerance that constrains the deviation features constructed about an axis or at right angles to an axis. It constrains the deviation over a surface with respect to a datum axis about which the part is rotated. The tolerance is applied simultaneously to all measuring positions as the part is rotated 360 degrees. Unless otherwise specified the rules governing total run-out tolerance defined in ISO 1101 shall apply. &lt;note&gt;Alternatively total run-out tolerance can be used according to the specifications given in ASME Y14.5.&lt;/note&gt; The set of referenced datums shall contain one revolute surface feature. The tolerance zone is limited either by: &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;two coaxial cylinders with a difference in radii equal to the tolerance value. In this case, the axis of the cylinders shall be the axis of the revolute surface feature, and the ideal feature corresponding to the toleranced surface is a cylinder;&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;two parallel planes separated by the distance specified by the tolerance value. In this case, the planes are perpendicular to the axis of the revolute surface feature, and the ideal feature corresponding to the toleranced surface is a plane.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>TotalRunoutTolerance</name>
      <ownedRule xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1677222900725_765902_154509" xmi:uuid="9de5b277-1285-4d73-bbc0-131029c91f9d" xmi:type="uml:Constraint">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1677222985461_643666_154521" xmi:uuid="41b5a99e-46ca-4961-a8d9-0e512a9f2d93" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1677223001509_340196_154522" xmi:uuid="6645c4fc-ebf7-4b7a-aa4e-617606c970d9" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//GeometricTolerance[substring-after(@xsi:type,':')='TotalRunoutTolerance']/Angle"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="../@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="unitRef" value="./Unit/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="//Unit[@uid=$unitRef]/Quantity/ClassString ='plane angle'"&gt;(TotalRunoutTolerance &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) The unit of Angle shall be a plane angle measure unit. &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1677222942582_181537_154511" xmi:uuid="d8a9d357-0556-49e8-b48b-169f46710df7" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1677222900725_765902_154509"/>
          <body>the unit of Angle shall be a plane angle measure unit. </body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>WR1</name>
        <constrainedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052857_312768_101018"/>
        <specification xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1677222900726_477457_154510" xmi:uuid="e356045c-5368-4bfc-9369-f5cb0b83d258" xmi:type="uml:OpaqueExpression">
          <body>self.Angle.Unit.oclAsType(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CommonResources::Unit).Quantity.oclAsType(Application_protocols::AP242::Domain_model::CommonResources::ClassStringProxy).value ='plane angle'</body>
          <language>OCL2.0</language>
        </specification>
      </ownedRule>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052940_630667_102136" xmi:uuid="b0f108b8-e871-4022-a533-630b6fafce6f" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
        <general xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052786_418916_100634"/>
      </generalization>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052811_84668_100741" xmi:uuid="f4205ca0-7315-46b9-af9e-9cbb6fa1f867" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1608111427122_250578_95076" xmi:uuid="d2467b02-cf1c-4a6b-907a-f87ab616e02f" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052811_84668_100741"/>
          <body>specifies the role of the DatumSystem for the TotalRunoutTolerance.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>DatumSystem</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052887_745486_101391"/>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052954_276163_102669"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
      <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052952_290551_102581" xmi:uuid="f59a0766-2ca7-4c0d-9502-62996e1d85ca" xmi:type="uml:Property">
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1608111434514_772791_95077" xmi:uuid="a97ddd89-596a-46f4-b11b-bd985145e92e" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052952_290551_102581"/>
          <body>the direction with respect to the datum axis in which a runout tolerance is controlled. The value of this attribute need not be specified.</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <name>Angle</name>
        <visibility>public</visibility>
        <type href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193283_976319_23905"/>
        <lowerValue xmi:id="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052951_269660_102559" xmi:uuid="f7aa15fe-ed2a-4fc0-a15f-7cd320237945" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger"/>
        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
        <association xmi:idref="_18_4_1_af4021f_1601394052937_346063_102052"/>
      </ownedAttribute>
    </packagedElement>
