            <body>&lt;sch:rule context="//GeometricTolerance[AreaUnitType='cylindrical']"&gt; &lt;sch:let name="uid" value="@uid"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="firstUnitSizeRef" value="./FirstUnitSize/Unit/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="isFirstUnitSizeLength" value="//Unit[@uid=$firstUnitSizeRef]/Quantity/ClassString ='length'"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="secondUnitSizeRef" value="./SecondUnitSize/Unit/@uidRef"/&gt; &lt;sch:let name="isSecondUnitSizePlaneAngle" value="//Unit[@uid=$secondUnitSizeRef]/Quantity/ClassString ='plane angle'"/&gt; &lt;sch:assert test="$isFirstUnitSizeLength and $isSecondUnitSizePlaneAngle"&gt;(GeometricTolerance &lt;sch:value-of select="$uid"/&gt;) If the AreaUnitType is cylindrical, the FirstUnitSize shall be a length measure and the SecondUnitSize shall be a value of plane angle measure. &lt;/sch:assert&gt; &lt;/sch:rule&gt;</body>
          </ownedComment>
          <body>Schematron</body>
        </ownedComment>
        <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_91401df_1614678721696_130131_91158" xmi:uuid="df43b6e7-3fd7-4c8f-a150-88d508644d50" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_91401df_1614678442454_680555_91156"/>
          <body>if the AreaUnitType is cylindrical, the FirstUnitSize shall be a length measure and the SecondUnitSize shall be a value of plane angle measure.</body>
        </ownedComment>
